    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nExcellent modern built - 3 bed Semi-detached house in exceptional conditionSpacious living accommodation throughout, c.105sqmModern shaker oakwood Kitchen with open plan diningSeparate living room to the front with bay windowLarge main bedroom with built in wardrobes and ensuite showerGas central heating and double-glazed windowsPrivate railed front garden with designated parking to the frontPrivate rear garden with extensive patio and covered inside entrance located within quiet modern cul de sac, close to Balbriggan town centreModern development which is close to the beach, harbour and all town centre amenitiesMinutes' drive to M1 motor giving easy access to Dublin Airport and city centre\n\nSituated within a peaceful and highly sought-after cul-de-sac in the modern Castleland Park View development, No. 60 is an exceptional three-bedroom semi-detached residence presented in superb turnkey condition. Beautifully maintained and thoughtfully designed, this impressive home extends to approximately 105 sq.m. (1,130 sq.ft.) of bright, spacious accommodation, offering the perfect balance of contemporary style, comfort and practicality for modern family living.\nUpon entering, you are welcomed by a bright entrance hall leading to a beautifully proportioned living room positioned to the front of the property. A striking bay window floods the room with natural light, creating a warm and inviting space for relaxation or entertaining. To the rear, the heart of the home is undoubtedly the stylish open-plan kitchen and dining area, featuring an elegant shaker-style oak kitchen with generous storage and workspace. This light-filled space seamlessly connects with the rear garden, making it ideal for both everyday family life and entertaining guests.\nUpstairs, the accommodation continues to impress with three generously sized bedrooms. The spacious principal bedroom benefits from built-in wardrobes and a contemporary en-suite shower room, while the remaining bedrooms are equally well-appointed and serviced by a modern family bathroom.\nOutside, the property enjoys a private railed front garden with designated off-street parking. To the rear, a beautifully enclosed garden offers a wonderful outdoor retreat, complete with an extensive patio area perfect for al fresco dining and entertaining, together with the added convenience of a covered side entrance providing practical storage and easy access.\nFurther enhancing the appeal of this outstanding home are gas-fired central heating, double-glazed windows throughout and an exceptional standard of presentation that allows the next owner to simply move in and enjoy.\nCastleland Park View is a highly regarded modern development ideally positioned just minutes from Balbriggan town centre, where a superb range of shops, cafés, restaurants, schools and leisure facilities are all within easy reach. The picturesque beach, harbour and scenic coastal walks are also close by, offering an enviable lifestyle combining coastal charm with everyday convenience. Excellent transport links include Balbriggan Train Station and the nearby M1 motorway, providing swift access to Dublin Airport, the M50 and Dublin City Centre, making this an ideal location for commuters.\nNo. 60 Castleland Park View represents a rare opportunity to acquire an impeccably presented family home in one of Balbriggan's most desirable residential developments, where quality, location and lifestyle come together to create a truly exceptional property."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - \nwith tiled flooring and understairs storage\n\nGuest WC - \nwith tiled flooring and w.c, w.h.b and storage unit\n\nLiving Room - \nwith wood flooring, bay window, open fire with timber surround and solid hearth, double doors to kitchen diner\n\nKitchen Area - \nwith tiled flooring, modern shaker oakwood units with breakfast bar and French doors to the rear\n\nDining area - \nOpen plan with kitchen and access to rear garden\n\nLanding - \nwith large hot press with storage and attic hatch\n\nBedroom One - \nLarge double room with built in wardrobes and ensuite shower room\n\nBedroom Two - \nDouble bedroom with build in wardrobes\n\nBedroom Three - \nDouble bedroom to the rear of the property\n\nFamily bathroom - \nwith full tiling and bath with shower over, w.c and w.h.b.\n\n"
      },
